fix: handle empty sessionStorage value to prevent JSON parse error
Fixes an "Unexpected end of JSON input" crash that occurs when navigating to `/extension/meshmap?mode=design` in design mode.
Root Cause
In ui/pages/_app.tsx, the `loadAbility` function reads `keys` from `sessionStorage` and passes it directly to `JSON.parse`:
const storedKeys = sessionStorage.getItem('keys');
if (storedKeys !== null && !reFetchKeys && storedKeys !== 'undefined') {
setState((prevState) => ({ ...prevState, keys: JSON.parse(storedKeys) }));
sessionStorage.getItem('keys') can return an empty string "" in edge cases (e.g., race condition on page load, or a corrupt prior session). The guard checked for null and "undefined" but not for an empty string — and JSON.parse("") throws "Unexpected end of JSON input", crashing the page.

fix(server): return error if any query fails in GetMeshSyncResourcesSummary
`GetMeshSyncResourcesSummary` runs 3 database queries but only returned an error if the first two BOTH failed. If only one failed, or if the labels query failed, the error was silently ignored and incomplete data was returned to the user with no warning.
Changed `&&` to `||` in the error condition to catch any query failure
Included all three errors (`err1`, `err2`, `err`) in the combined error message for better debugging
Removed misleading comment "only return error if both queries failed"
Before
// only return error if both queries failed
if err1 != nil && err2 != nil {
combinedErr := fmt.Errorf("error fetching meshsync resources summary: %v, %v", err1, err2)
After
// return error if any query failed
if err1 != nil || err2 != nil || err != nil {
combinedErr := fmt.Errorf("error fetching meshsync resources summary: kinds_err=%v, namespaces_err=%v, labels_err=%v", err1, err2, err)

fix: prevent nil pointer panic in ErrBlankName
`ErrBlankName` in `server/handlers/error.go` unconditionally calls `err.Error()` on its argument. Both call sites in `load_test_handler.go` always pass a `nil` error because all non-nil error paths return early before the blank name check is reached. This causes a runtime nil pointer dereference panic when a load test is submitted with a blank name.
Root Cause
// Before fix
func ErrBlankName(err error) error {
return errors.New(ErrBlankNameCode, errors.Alert,
[]string{"Error: name field is blank."},
At both call sites (`LoadTestUsingSMPHandler` line 66 and `RunLoadTestHandler` line 251), the `err` variable is always `nil` when the blank name condition is hit — prior non-nil errors cause early returns.
Fix
Replaced `err.Error()` with a hardcoded inline description string. Since both call sites always pass `nil`, the dynamic `err.Error()` was providing no useful information. Using an inline literal also satisfies the `errorutil` static analyzer which requires all `errors.New()` arguments to be inline literals.
// After fix
func ErrBlankName(err error) error {
return errors.New(ErrBlankNameCode, errors.Alert,
[]string{"Error: name field is blank."},
Submit a load test request (SMP or form-based) with a blank `name` field
Before fix: server panics
After fix: server returns a proper `403 Forbidden` with the blank name error message
