[Server] Restrict URL imports to public destinations with size and time limits
Importing a design or filter by URL (`POST /api/filter` with `url`) fetched the address with a bare `http.Get` and an unbounded `io.ReadAll`. The server could be made to reach loopback, cluster-internal or cloud-metadata addresses, and to buffer an arbitrarily large or never-ending response.
What changed
New `server/models/remote_file_fetch.go`. `genericHTTPFilterFile` and `genericHTTPPatternFile` now fetch through it. The client:
allows only `http`/`https`, including on redirects, and follows at most 5 redirects;
refuses non-public addresses in the dialer's `Control` hook (loopback, RFC 1918/ULA, link-local incl. `169.254.169.254`, CGNAT, multicast, unspecified, reserved, IPv4-mapped IPv6). Checking the IP actually dialled covers every redirect hop and DNS rebinding, which a pre-check of the URL host would not;
does not use environment proxies (through a proxy the dialer only sees the proxy address, so the check would not apply to the real destination);
has a 30s timeout and reads at most 10 MiB.
New opt-in `ALLOW_PRIVATE_REMOTE_FILE_IMPORTS` (default `false`) for operators who import from hosts on a private network. Documented in `environment-variables.md`.
Tests: `server/models/remote_file_fetch_test.go` (address classification, loopback rejected without reaching the server, scheme rejection, size limit incl. at-limit, timeout, redirect limit, redirect to a non-public hop refused, opt-in). `TestFilterPOSTResponseCarriesURLImportedFilter` imports from a loopback `httptest`
